UID:99b2ba54757f82cf@role-environmental-land-use.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260928T231444Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260928
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] October 2026
DESCRIPTION:O&M Newsletter\, October 2026\nMaine Department of Environment
 al Protection sent this bulletin at 09/28/2026 11:57 AM EDT\nOCTOBER 2026\
 nIn this issue:\nDon't Miss Out: Participate in the FREE EPA Cybersecurity
  Series Today.\nCelebrating the Retirement of Two Dedicated DEP Employees 
 This October.\nDMR-QA Study 46 Open!\nTraining Highlights.\nIndustry Profi
 le: James Galasyn Serving 40 years in the Environmental Laboratory Field.\
 nCelebrating Innovative Water Professionals.\nFor Practice.\nDon't Miss Ou
 t: Participate in the FREE EPA Cybersecurity Series Today.\nCheck out the 
 October schedule for this comprehensive line-up of no-cost EPA Cybersecuri
 ty Webinars.\nCybersecurity 102\n- October 6\, 2026. Take a deeper look at
  Operational Technology (OT) cybersecurity and learn practical steps for n
 avigating today’s threats.\nCybersecurity 103\n- October 8\, 2026. Under
 stand current threats\, risks\, and vulnerabilities facing water systems a
 nd how to stay informed.\nCybersecurity 104\n- October 13\, 2026. Get simp
 le\, low‑cost best practices tailored for small and resource‑constrain
 ed utilities.\nCybersecurity Refresher\n- October 15\, 2026. Reinforce fou
 ndational concepts from Cyber 101\, 102\, and 103.\nCybersecurity 201\n- O
 ctober 20\, 2026. Explore how AI supports defenders and attackers—and le
 arn how to use it safely.\nCybersecurity 202\n- October 22\, 2026. Learn p
 ractical Zero Trust steps to strengthen access controls and protect Inform
 ation Technology (IT)/Operational Technology (OT) environments.\nWater Cyb
 ersecurity Assessment Tool (WCAT) Webinar\n- October 27\, 2026. See how EP
 A's WCAT can assess cybersecurity gaps at water and wastewater systems.\nC
 ybersecurity Procurement Checklist Tool Training\n- October 28\, 2026. Lea
 rn how to evaluate vendors using EPA’s procurement checklist.\nCybersecu
 rity 203\n- October 29\, 2026. Identify and reduce risks from vendors\, co
 ntractors\, and other third parties.\nCelebrating the Retirement of Two De
 dicated DEP Employees This October.\nGary Brooks - Eastern Maine Complian\
 nhttps://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/MEDEP/bulletins/42c5d6a
URL:https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/MEDEP/bulletins/42c5d6a
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
